 "findings": [
  {
   "class": "other",
   "file": "plugins/specclaw/tests/run-infosec-evals.sh",
   "fp": "0828002f11b7",
   "in_delta": true,
   "line": 71,
   "message": "`review()` ignores `claude`'s exit code (`|| true`) and drops stderr (`2>/dev/null`). Any stdout from a failed call is scored as a real report. With `--max-turns 1` and an agent that has the Write tool, the CLI can exit non-zero and still print a text error. That error is counted as an answered call with no findings: a miss on `vulnerable` and 'no false alarm' on `fixed`. Fix: capture the exit status and treat any non-zero exit as no answer. Add a stub row that prints text and exits 1. The current `STUB_FAIL` row exits 0 with empty output, so it only covers the empty case.",
   "original_severity": "major",
   "pass": "review",
   "pre_existing": false,
   "rule": "B3",
   "scenario": "The CLI hits max turns or a quota error, prints 'Error: Reached max turns (1)' to stdout and exits 1. The runner counts the call as answered with no findings, so a run where nothing was reviewed reports `False-alarm rate: 0%` and exits 0.",
   "severity": "major",
   "unclassified": false
  },
  {
   "class": "other",
   "file": ".github/workflows/infosec-evals.yml",
   "fp": "7730dd9de63d",
   "in_delta": true,
   "line": 20,
   "message": "The nightly default is still the alias `sonnet`, and the runner records it as given (`**Model:** sonnet`). The CLI is installed unpinned (`npm install -g @anthropic-ai/claude-code`) and its version is not recorded. The persisted result therefore does not record which model or CLI produced it. Fix: default to a full model ID, or record the resolved model the CLI reports (e.g. with `--output-format json`). Pin the CLI version or record `claude --version` in the result header.",
   "original_severity": "major",
   "pass": "review",
   "pre_existing": false,
   "rule": "B5",
   "scenario": "The `sonnet` alias moves to a new model between two nightly runs. Both result files read `**Model:** sonnet` with different catch rates, so a regression cannot be told apart from a model swap.",
   "severity": "major",
   "unclassified": false
  },
  {
   "class": "other",
   "file": "plugins/specclaw/tests/run-infosec-evals.sh",
   "fp": "66f8a308d008",
   "in_delta": true,
   "line": 85,
   "message": "When `expect` is missing or has no `rule:` line, `want` is empty. The regex `\\b()\\b` then matches any finding heading, so any finding counts as a catch. Only the separate structural suite guards this. Fix: fail the case when `want` is empty.",
   "original_severity": "minor",
   "pass": "review",
   "pre_existing": false,
   "rule": "B6",
   "scenario": "",
   "severity": "minor",
   "unclassified": false
  },
  {
   "class": "other",
   "file": "plugins/specclaw/tests/evals/infosec/session-after-logout/fixed.js",
   "fp": "1c86eb12ab97",
   "in_delta": true,
   "line": 1,
   "message": "The 'fixed' password-change route does not ask for the current password before setting a new one. A correct reviewer may flag this as an account-takeover weakness on the fixed sample. The case is also named 'after-logout' but tests a password change. Fix: require and verify `req.body.currentPassword`, and rename the case to match.",
   "original_severity": "minor",
   "pass": "review",
   "pre_existing": false,
   "rule": "B6",
   "scenario": "",
   "severity": "minor",
   "unclassified": false
  },
  {
   "class": "other",
   "file": "plugins/specclaw/references/full/plan.md",
   "fp": "2cceb4f6acf1",
   "in_delta": true,
   "line": 27,
   "message": "The spike skip condition says the change is a spike when `specclaw-validate-change ... status` prints `Size:`. Every change prints `Size:`, so read literally the step skips for all changes. Fix: say it prints `Size: spike`.",
   "original_severity": "minor",
   "pass": "review",
   "pre_existing": false,
   "rule": "B1",
   "scenario": "",
   "severity": "minor",
   "unclassified": false
  },
  {
   "class": "other",
   "file": "plugins/specclaw/tests/run-infosec-eval-cases-tests.sh",
   "fp": "c3b9acad46b4",
   "in_delta": true,
   "line": 61,
   "message": "The check 'the runner leaves tests/results alone when told to write elsewhere' only confirms that a file exists in `$TMP/results`. It never checks that `tests/results` is unchanged, so the name claims more than the test proves. Fix: snapshot `tests/results` before and after the run and compare.",
   "original_severity": "minor",
   "pass": "review",
